      "message": "Thanks for the review. I don\u0027t have access to XDPE1x2xx hardware, so I can\u0027t\nprovide an end-to-end Redfish test on a real VR.\n\nThe change is limited to parseImage(), which runs in verifyImage() before any\nI2C write. It now returns false when the \"[End Configuration Data]\" marker is\nmissing or no configuration sections were parsed. Valid images follow the same\npath as before.\n\nCould someone with an XDPE platform run the Redfish update with:\n 1. a valid config image: update succeeds, as before\n 2. an image with \"[End Configuration Data]\" removed: update fails with\n    \"Failed to parse a complete XDPE configuration image\", VR version unchanged\n 3. an image with no configuration data rows: same failure, version unchanged\n\nIf hardware testing isn\u0027t possible, I can add a unit test for parseImage()\ncovering valid, truncated and empty images.",
